From a8319f32d4968bd385e5a0db5925653275171c27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:27:25 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] TEST ONLY: minimal fbdev driver on the handed-over A50
 display pipeline (do not merge)

M7.2 boot D2a. a50-decon keeps the command-mode DECON state that S-Boot
leaves (D0c) and provides an fbdev device on the boot framebuffer, one
frame per FBIOPAN_DISPLAY (the D1 trigger sequence, masked again on frame
done), TE vsync timestamps in the platform device's "vsync" attribute while
S3CFB_SET_VSYNC_INT is on, and no-op S3CFB_POWER_MODE/FBIOBLANK.
S3CFB_WIN_CONFIG follows in D2b.

exynos9610-a50-d2.dts is the M6.3 SysMMU test DT with simplefb disabled
and a decon_f@148b0000 node (stock DECON registers, IRQs, TE gpc2-3,
DISPAUD and DPU SysMMU clocks, the reserved boot framebuffer).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I4f9164d4afb679f2d2764acf84e79bd0e704f038
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/Makefile           |   1 +
 .../boot/dts/exynos/exynos9610-a50-d2.dts     |  37 ++
 drivers/video/fbdev/Makefile                  |   1 +
 drivers/video/fbdev/a50-decon.c               | 372 ++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 411 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9610-a50-d2.dts
 create mode 100644 drivers/video/fbdev/a50-decon.c

